    "created_at": "2018-01-31T19:01:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-31T19:01:06Z",
    "body": "Ok, good.\r\n\r\nI don't know if its a problem, but the cross-origin blob URLs also kind of leak some information about when the creating context goes away.  If thats like a nested context that the current origin wouldn't know about it might be some kind of cross-origin information leakage.  Kind of weak, but nice to avoid.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
